        <argsstring>(const XAsu_SlhdsaSignVerifyParams *ParamsPtr)</argsstring>
        <name>XAsu_SlhdsaValidateSignVerifyParams</name>
        <param>
          <type>const <ref refid="struct_x_asu___slhdsa_sign_verify_params" kindref="compound">XAsu_SlhdsaSignVerifyParams</ref> *</type>
          <declname>ParamsPtr</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>This function validates SLH-DSA signature verification parameters. </para>        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>ParamsPtr</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Pointer to <ref refid="struct_x_asu___slhdsa_sign_verify_params" kindref="compound">XAsu_SlhdsaSignVerifyParams</ref>.</para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>XST_SUCCESS, if validation succeeds.</para></listitem><listitem><para>XST_INVALID_PARAM, if any field is invalid (NULL pointer, zero addresses, invalid ParamSet, CtxLen/CtxAddr mismatch, MsgLen exceeds DMA limit, SignatureLen mismatch, or PubKeyLen not equal to the ParamSet public key size). </para></listitem></itemizedlist>
</para></simplesect>
</para>        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
<para>Validate input pointer.</para><para>Validate the parameter set, which fixes the expected signature and public key sizes.</para><para>Validate the context length against the FIPS 205 limit of 255 bytes.</para><para>Validate that a context address is supplied whenever a non-empty context is used. Both CtxLen and CtxAddr must reproduce the values used at signing time, because the context is bound into the message digest.</para><para>Bound the message length by the maximum single ASU DMA transfer length.</para><para>The public key, message and signature addresses are all mandatory for verification.</para><para>Reject a signature whose length does not match the parameter set, so that a truncated or oversized signature is never parsed as if it were well formed.</para><para>The public key is a fixed length per parameter set, so PubKeyLen must match exactly. Verification always reads the whole key, so a shorter declared length would leave part of it unvalidated.</para><para>Validate the message mode and, for pre-hash mode, the HashId and digest length. </para>        </inbodydescription>
